{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["And Scripture said of Aaron's tunic at the beginning: <b>וכתנת תשבץ</b> (above, Exodus 28:4) — that it alone is brocaded, and not so the tunics of his sons; and the brocade is made for Aaron's honor. Thus it says in the account of the rite: <b>ויתן עליו הכתנת</b> (Leviticus 8:7) — the known one, which is the brocaded one; and of his sons: <b>וילבישם כתנות</b> (there, verse 13), like <b>ולבני אהרן תעשה כתנות</b> (below, verse 40). And Rav Saadia translated <b>ושבצת</b> — it is like the shape of a coin, square, made within the circle."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The citation '(למעלה פ' ד)' resolves to Exodus 28:4, as this commentary is on Exodus 28."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:54.674616002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}